        "narrative": "<p>INTRODUCTORY STOCKING IN 1985 THROUGH 1987 SUCCEEDED IN ESTABLISHING FAIR NUMBERS OF WAE. ALTHOUGH SURVIVAL OF THE 1985 STOCKING WAS APPARENTLY LOW, THE 1986 AND 1987 STOCKING SHOWED GOOD SURVIVAL AND GAST GROWTH.  THERE WAS NO EVIDENCE OF ANY NATURAL REPRODUCTION; HOWEVER, WAE WERE PROBABLY JUST REACHING MATURITY.  NOP ABUNDANCE WAS GOOD, BUT NO FISH OVER 22 IN WERE COLLECTED.  SEVERAL YEAR CLASSES WERE REPRESENTED AND GROWTH WAS AVERAGE FOR COOK COUNTY.  FORAGE FOR GAME FISH APPEARED TO BE LIMITED.  ONLY ONE YEP WAS COLLECTED AND THE WHITE SUCKER COLLECTED WERE TOO LARGE TO SERVE AS FORAGE FOR THE SIZE NOP PRESENT.</p>",
