        "narrative": "<p>The walleye catch was very low, as it has always been in this lake.  Survival of stocked walleye fry has apparently been very poor.  Growth rates of the two walleye caught appear to have been normal for the area.The northern pike catch was slightly low for this lake, but ranked above the median for the lake class.  Average size was small for the lake, and somewhat small for the lake class, because pike older than age 4 were not caught.  Growth rates had been normal for the area.Yellow perch abundance remained relatively low.  One perch caught was probably large enough to have been of interest to anglers.White sucker abundance at the time of sampling could be considered medium, but average size of suckers was larger than in most similar lakes.</p>",
